					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-20 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>chunk a deuce, pahtnah!&nbsp; take a lint roller to that musty-ass <strong>members only</strong> jacket and get suited up for tonight&#39;s medicinal goodness at the chop.&nbsp; fuck what the <strong>Times</strong> say - with all the talent this bill has to offer i&#39;m bettin&#39; the line backs up to AT LEAST <strong>piecora&#39;s</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp; and when the <strong>guns</strong> is in the house, oh my god...<br /><br />anybody catch ya bwoy <strong>sabzi</strong> last night on the 11 o&#39;clock news?&nbsp; evidently he&#39;s been part-timing at <strong>huling bros</strong>.&nbsp; nah -- for real though, he was doin&#39; the damn thing for the sake of the kids (if nothing more) at <strong>EMP</strong>, schoolin&#39; young bucks on the ways of the come-up.&nbsp; good on ya, cousin.<br /><br />i&#39;m becoming awfully suspicious of <strong>VH1&#39;s white rapper show.</strong>&nbsp; not for any reason steeped in half-hearted socio-political nonsense, but because <strong>ego trip&#39;s</strong> got too much hood cred to really let this thing come off like another season of <strong>the real world</strong>.&nbsp; i&#39;m bettin&#39; a cup of <strong>joe bar&#39;s</strong> finest that the one crowned king of caucasians is in for a big (book of) surprise when they find out <strong>THERE IS NO MONEY</strong>.&nbsp; showin&#39; these scrappers what it&#39;s like to be hustled, humiliated and commodified&nbsp;&nbsp;would be a lesson worth more than millions.&nbsp; now that&#39;s KILLER!!<br /><br />see y&#39;all in the sewer -- i mean the suey.<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-18 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>?good watts.<br /><br />it&#39;s slightly warmer.  the two foot icicles hanging from my house have now liquidated themselves and returned to the earth from whence they came.<br /><br />ahem.<br /><br />this weekend is gonna be full of activity.<br /><br /><strong>Grammy Career Day 2007</strong> tomorrow at the <strong>EMP</strong> should prove to be an interesting event.  i&#39;ll be there facilitating a <strong>&quot;How I Make Beats&quot; workshop</strong> around lunchtime with a projector hooked up to the computer.  <br /><br />later that day, if you happen to be in <strong>Corvallis, OR</strong> in the evening, you&#39;ll be able to catch the <strong>Native Guns</strong> and <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> doin a little somethin somethin at <strong>Oregon State University</strong>.<br /><br />saturday, i&#39;ll be at <strong>my uncle&#39;s house</strong> in <strong>Renton, WA</strong> kickin <strong>it</strong> with fam in honor of <strong>my cousin</strong> visiting from <strong>Beijing</strong>.  that&#39;s not really a public event, so i&#39;m not sure why i&#39;m <strong>bolding the pronouns</strong>, but don&#39;t trip cuz at that same time, your boys <strong>Good Medicine</strong> will be rocking the stage with <strong>Native Guns</strong> and a plethora of local talent at <strong>Chop Suey</strong>.  GO TO THAT.<br /><br />for those who decided to watch <strong>American Idol</strong> (Seattle auditions) last night, you might have noticed that, as usual, the mainstream media has an affinity for bad-mouthing our beloved Town.  &quot;<strong>Seattle ain&#39;t sh**!</strong>&quot; was the prevailing theme of the show.  i personally take offense to this, although i&#39;m not particularly surprised.  oh well.<br /><br /><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/bleezy.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />some of you may have recognized former Seattle <strong>SCIONtific Records Beat Box Competition</strong> champion <strong>BShorty</strong> (alias <strong>Blake Lewis</strong>) holdin it down claimin &quot;Emerald City!&quot; throughout his audition.  good luck brosef.  do yo&#39; thing.<br /><br />-sabarillo-<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-17 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>as shalom ashanti, company.&nbsp; i&#39;m hoping this reprieve from frozen precipitation brings warmth to your heart as well as your block...<br /><br />speakin&#39; of heat - big shouts out to the local beatmakers who keep blessin&#39; me with the goodness.&nbsp; thanks to <strong>flowside, MTK, infi-note, khazma, Cin7, seance</strong> and a full clip of others.&nbsp; nearly 6 weeks after takin&#39; one helluva loss in san fran, i&#39;ve re-upped somethin&#39; marvelous.&nbsp; the pen is hot, y&#39;all - keep both eyes open for compilations and mixtapes set to drop in the very near future...<br /><br />and speakin&#39; of the future - as i understand it, in 2009 women will inexplicably become completely infertile.&nbsp; word up - not a single child will be born for 18 years causing the world (but particularly england) to be stricken with fear, distress and depression.&nbsp; if you think that&#39;s disturbing, you should see how first-world immigration policies evolve.&nbsp; if you wanna see more - get to a theater near you and peep <strong>children of men</strong> - it&#39;s that shit!<br /><br />and speaking of shit - check for tonight&#39;s episode of <strong>american idol</strong> - it&#39;s the town&#39;s night to clown.&nbsp; i&#39;m watchin&#39; for the sake of my dude <strong>b-shorty</strong> - rumor has it his bags are packed for hollywood.&nbsp; take one for the team, fam...<br /><br />be good.<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-16 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>This Saturday ya&#39;ll... <strong><a href="http://www.nativeguns.com/" target="_blank">Native Guns</a></strong> are back in Seattle for the first time since the MassLine launch party last summer, along with only the 2nd <strong>Good Medicine</strong> performance ever!&nbsp; And did I hear you say something about <strong>Yirim Seck</strong>?&nbsp; check his crew <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iEuFKX6nFG0" target="_blank"><strong>Pyrate Radio&#39;s</strong> video here</a>... and get those tickets fast at <a href="http://www.ticketweb.com/user/?region=wa&amp;query=detail&amp;event=709373" target="_blank">Ticketweb.com</a>&nbsp; <br /><br /><strong>Lovework</strong> has been getting more amazing reviews left &amp; right... along with being in <strong>URB Magazine</strong> this month, check out what <strong><a href="http://www.shotgunreviews.com/reviews/music/hiphop/#gabrielteodros_lovework" target="_blank">Shotgun Reviews</a></strong> had to say, they&#39;ll have an interview up soon as well.&nbsp; The <strong>national release date is set for February 27th</strong>, but you&nbsp;get your first chance&nbsp;pick up the album at the <strong>Chop Suey</strong> on <strong><a href="http://www.ticketweb.com/user/?region=wa&amp;query=detail&amp;event=708011" target="_blank">February 24th</a></strong>.&nbsp; <br /><br /><strong>Khingz Makoma</strong> of Abyssinian Creole has been mad busy lately as well, after just releasing the amazing&nbsp;<strong>Hillionaire Boys Club MxTape</strong> only 2 months ago, he just finished recording for <strong>Khingz County</strong>, a new mx-tape featuring the South End&#39;s finest lyricist rockin beats from the late-great <strong>J Dilla</strong>.&nbsp; Lookout for both projects at an <strong>Ab Creole</strong> show near you... your mom loves em.<br /><br />Other then that, we&#39;ve just been enjoying good food at the <strong>Hidmo</strong>, driving carefully over this ice, and i&#39;ve been completely inspired by the future of hiphop... peace to <strong>Canary Sing</strong>, <strong>Muridian</strong>, <strong>Language Artz</strong> and <strong>El Dia</strong>.&nbsp; Ya&#39;ll make me proud to represent Seattle.<br /><br />and some of that art ya&#39;ll have been posting in <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=384.msg9647#msg9647" target="_blank">the forums</a> is dooope.<br /><br />peace fam<br />-- gtzi<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-15 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><span class="body1 style73">it is COLD brosef. the oil ran out in
my house so my son and i have been crowding around the baseboard heater
trying to stay warm and cooking grilled cheese sandwiches with a
clothes iron.<br /><br />sike.  i don&#39;t have a son.  but the house is cold.<br /><br />big up to all the folks that rocked the <strong>MLK Hip Hop Show&nbsp;</strong> at<strong>Youngstown</strong> on <strong>Delridge</strong> last Saturday.  i swung thru for a minute to see some different folkers rockin the stage including <strong>Rajnii Eddins</strong>,<strong> Scribes</strong>, some cats from <strong>Youthspeaks</strong>, <strong>WD40</strong> (who&#39;s skratching and mixing are topped only by his excellent espresso) and your boys from <strong>Abyssinian Creole</strong>.<br /><br />oh, and peace to <strong>Jelani</strong>.  he&#39;s filthy.<br /><br />even more bigs and ups and big ups to the folkers that rocked the <strong>Make It Or Break It</strong> joint last night at <strong>Chop Suey</strong>.  i hear that it was the debut performance of some of our very own MassLine forumsters.  holla!<br /><br /><br />it is <strong>Monday, January 15th</strong>.  happy born day to <strong>Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr.</strong>  ya&#39;ll might catch some of us MassLine Representatives at the<strong> Seattle MLK Rally</strong> and march beginning at <strong>Franklin High School</strong>, 3013 S. Mount Baker Blvd. at 11am.<br /><br />stay warm.<br /><br /></span><span class="body1 style73">Saba</span><br /><span class="body1 style73"><br /><br />&quot;The
problem of racism, the problem of economic exploitation, and the
problem of war are all tied together. These are the triple evils that
are interrelated.&quot;<br /><br />The Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr.<br /><br /><br /></span><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[4